## Memory model (Safety-critical)

Principles only — check patterns and InfoSys evidence: `rules/twincat3-pagefault-safety.mdc` · skill `twincat3-pagefault-audit`. Dynamic string/`__NEW` workflows: skill `twincat3-json-strings`.

- No dynamic memory by default. Variables are allocated at compile time.
- Arrays have fixed size. No resizable containers. Always check index bounds before write/read when the index is not a proven constant range.
- Dynamic allocation: `__NEW` / `__DELETE` (InfoSys; router memory) — project convention: prefer for JSON/IoT payloads. Always validate `<> 0`, delete exactly once, no use-after-free, pair on all paths.
- `POINTER TO` / `REFERENCE TO` / interfaces: always validate before use; never assume validity across cycles when the referent can disappear.

